## Why This Is Asked
This probes cross-region real-time reliability, backpressure handling, and semantics trade-offs in a live data plane.

## Key Concepts
- Tail latency monitoring; regional failover
- Backpressure and traffic shaping
- Exactly-once vs at-least-once semantics
- Offset management and idempotent processing
- Chaos testing and post-incident reviews

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo idempotent replay handler
function processEvent(evt){
  const id = evt.id;
  if (processedSet.has(id)) return;
  store.update(evt.payload);
  processedSet.add(id);
  commitOffsets(evt.offset);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate this plan with simulated regional outages?
- What telemetry would you add to quantify readiness and bottlenecks?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical SRE skills: incident triage, region-aware rollouts, backpressure, circuit breaking, and rollback discipline beyond basic incident response.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-region latency analysis
- Cache stampede mitigation
- Per-region deployment strategies (canary, rollouts)
- Safe rollback criteria and instrumentation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple circuit breaker (pseudo)
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold) { this.open = false; this.failures = 0; this.threshold = threshold; }
  onFailure() { this.failures++; if (this.failures > this.threshold) this.open = true; }
  allow() { return !this.open; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to a service mesh with traffic shifting?
- How would you verify rollback correctness across all regions post-incident?

